{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{artist: Robert Burns}
{genre: folk}
{tempo: 100}
# Historical Scots text (1788); traditional tune. First verse and chorus.
# Original simplified chord accompaniment for MooSic.
{c:Verse}
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [G]never brought to [C]mind?
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [C]auld lang [G]syne?

{c:Chorus}
For [G]auld lang [D]syne, my dear,
For [G]auld lang [C]syne,
We'll [G]tak a cup o' [D]kindness yet,
For [C]auld lang [G]syne.
